174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (Many hardworking groups were formed to bring to life this ambitious design. Some were assigned to the foundry, some to the woodworking, while others worked on the forged torsades, not to mention the machining of the cathedral-like piece. I handled the designing of the stained-glass shank as well as its painting, but also took part in the casting of the ZAMAC parts - an alloy similar to but easier to cast than aluminium and much denser - and the golden brass parts. In total, around 2,000 hours of craftsmanship work spent between January and June of 2025 to give this design a tangible form. The response was overwhelming, with the project generating tremendous excitement on LinkedIn and coverage in local newspapers.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
